# Netlify: the files in the published folder that are not part of the site, and the repository's
# own files should the checkout ever be published by mistake, answer the not-found page. `404!`
# rather than `404`: a plain rule is shadowed by a file at the same path, and these are files
# that can be there. Netlify never serves _headers or _redirects itself; they are listed so the
# three configurations refuse the same paths. Cloudflare Pages ignores 404 rules: there, publish
# the folder `npm run build:web` writes, which leaves metadata.json out.
/_headers        /404.html  404!
/_redirects      /404.html  404!
/.htaccess       /404.html  404!
/metadata.json   /404.html  404!
/README.md       /404.html  404!
/.git/*          /404.html  404!
/deploy/*        /404.html  404!
